{"id": "live-307", "title": "ACORE Capital Declares Default on GPI Companies' West End Office Campus", "category": "lending-foreclosure", "status": "filed", "date": "2026-10-12", "jurisdiction": "Los Angeles County, California (non-judicial trustee's sale)", "state": "CA", "amount": "More than $80M claimed owed; 2024 refinancing reported at $97.6M", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://therealdeal.com/la/2026/10/12/gpi-defaults-on-loan-faces-foreclosure-of-west-la-office-campus/", "summary": "ACORE Capital recorded a notice of default against developer GPI Companies in September 2026 over West End, a 235,000-square-foot creative office campus at 10730 West Pico Boulevard in West Los Angeles, built on the site of a shuttered Macy's at the former Westside Pavilion. The Real Deal reported the default on October 12, 2026, saying ACORE claims more than $80 million is owed; the campus, completed in 2022, reportedly remains entirely vacant.", "significance": "The default underscores how speculative creative-office conversions financed in the low-rate years before 2022 are colliding with a leasing market that has been slow to absorb new office product without a signed anchor tenant. Lenders and sponsors with similar vacant spec-office collateral nearing maturity should treat the case as a signal that lenders are moving to recorded defaults relatively quickly once a non-performing asset shows no credible near-term leasing path.", "judge": null, "tags": ["office", "notice-of-default", "foreclosure", "los-angeles", "creative-office"]}
